    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0409" n="319" xml:id="pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862t.01/69a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-08T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1920—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>713. Cable promptly and fully for our guidance your impressions of situation
                    arising out of the Ruhr Valley question, particularly the situation arising from
                    occupation by French forces of Frankfort and other cities. Also cable any
                    information you can obtain or have received in regard to actions which are
                    contemplated by other nations or communications which have been exchanged.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
